{"id":"supervision","ord":"a0","title":"The orchestrator","desc":"Coordinate authorized work through kolu lanes and bounded native investigations. This subtree is durable memory; the transcript is history.\n\nBoot, including after compaction: AGENTS.md → this subtree → the `lanes` conventions → active lane subtrees through MCP. Follow mirrors; load completed lanes only for relevant history. Read product docs when needed: ~/code/olai/docs/chat.md for chat/wakes and ~/code/olai/docs/format.md for addresses.\n\nBoot or rule edits alone do not authorize dispatch.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00","custom":{"chat-agent-session":"codex:01a08141-c109-74a3-b949-fa6723e5744d"}}
{"id":"ci-venue","parent":"dag","ord":"a1","title":"CI venue — the standing ruling","desc":"Platform selection, venue constraints and CI ownership are defined in `dag-pr-ci`; merge requirements are in `dag-pr-merge`.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-pr-process","parent":"dag","ord":"a2","title":"kolu PRs ride kolu's own process","desc":"Kolu uses its own /be process instead of the ordinary review round. Its author opens any required paired-drishti PR. The orchestrator owns CI through odu MCP; authors do not run /ci. Merge requires /be complete and both platforms green, subject to the CI hold.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-memory","parent":"orch-board-rules","ord":"a2","title":"Memory","desc":"Record verified standing facts and approved decisions at their owning node. Keep current snapshots; git keeps history. Use `orch-standing-memory` only when no existing node owns the fact. Routine maintenance is authorized; policy approval is separate.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:51-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-through-kolu","parent":"orch-loop","ord":"a2","title":"Implementation lanes use kolu","desc":"Durable authors use separate kolu worktrees; terminal reviewers use splits. Resolve terminal orders from board claims and use instant actions, not blocking supervision waits. Native investigations follow `orch-native-delegation`.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:53-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-wake","parent":"orch-loop","ord":"a0","title":"The wake mechanism","desc":"The human selects orchestrator/lanes.olai in terminal and CI wake pickers. Saved choices survive restart and compaction; never claim arming without evidence.\n\nOn a wake, inspect the current lane, deepest owning step and terminal/CI evidence. Reconcile, then advance authorized work or record a block. Avoid duplicate actions; unclaimed terminals belong to the human. Answer agent permissions only within the brief, worktree and your own authority. Report missing scopes once.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:56-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-nag","parent":"orch-loop","ord":"a1","title":"Nag discipline","desc":"Re-evaluate an unchanged block; act under standing authority or escalate instead of repeating acknowledgments. Dismiss events, not terminals.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:58-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-ban","parent":"orch-authority","ord":"a0","title":"THE BAN: no process changes without approval","desc":"Policy changes require explicit human approval. For a process failure, explain its cause and propose a fix before changing policy.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:59-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-reboot","parent":"orch-authority","ord":"a4","title":"Re-boot after compaction","desc":"Repeat the root node's boot chain after compaction, before acting on a lane. A conversation summary is a navigation aid, not current board evidence.","created":"2026-08-27T15:04:31-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-law-over-practice","parent":"orch-authority","ord":"a1","title":"Law over practice","desc":"Current explicit instructions override board defaults; higher-priority harness instructions remain binding. Habit and historical practice are not policy. Ask about genuine conflicts only when they block an action.","created":"2026-08-27T15:04:34-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-no-volatile","parent":"orch-board-rules","ord":"a1","title":"No volatile facts on the board","desc":"Keep decisions in notes and typed facts in properties. Read heads, CI and terminal state fresh; do not duplicate volatile progress in prose.","created":"2026-08-27T18:41:48-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-sweep","parent":"orch-board-rules","ord":"a3","title":"Sweep on every transition","desc":"On each transition, reconcile the whole lane subtree: marks, claims, notes, mirrors and edges. Compare actual terminal work with doing steps; repair mismatches using evidence.","created":"2026-08-27T18:41:50-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-no-law-in-repos","parent":"orch-authority","ord":"a3","title":"Process law never lives in product repos","desc":"Workflow policy belongs in this vault. Product repositories provide build commands and technical conventions; dispatch briefs govern the lane's process.","created":"2026-08-29T10:34:04-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-findings-inbox","parent":"orch-authority","ord":"a2","title":"Findings park in the Inbox, never only in chat","desc":"Put outstanding human decisions in the appropriate Inbox queue, marked todo, with owning-node and PR links where applicable. When resolved, preserve the decision at its owner and clear the queue.","created":"2026-08-29T11:39:59-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-mcp-only-reads","parent":"orch-board-rules","ord":"a0","title":"BANNED: reading .olai files outside the MCP","desc":"Read .olai content through MCP only; git history is the exception. Discover tool names and schemas. If MCP cannot answer the question, report the gap instead of using raw file reads.","created":"2026-08-29T15:01:02-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-authority","parent":"supervision","ord":"aE","title":"Authority","created":"2026-09-02T10:32:48-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-loop","parent":"supervision","ord":"aF","title":"The supervision loop","created":"2026-09-02T10:32:48-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-board-rules","parent":"supervision","ord":"aG","title":"The board: reading and writing","created":"2026-09-02T10:32:48-04:00"}
{"id":"agents-root","parent":"supervision","ord":"aI","title":"The roster","desc":"Use each roster command verbatim; refuse a spawn without one. Authors run in separate kolu worktrees; terminal reviewers use splits. The choosing node owns defaults. Historical kimi observations live in orchestrator/kimi-ledger.olai.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"claude-opus — the author agent","desc":"Opus with the 1M window. Verify the model at launch. Claude composer placeholders are not unsent human drafts.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions","concurrency":"HARD CAP: at most THREE concurrent Claude Opus AUTHOR lanes (daily-limit reasons); Opus REVIEWERS are exempt and do not count; grok/pi are outside the cap. The orchestrator queues further Opus work until a slot frees.","context":"1M — the [1m] suffix pins it everywhere (native on the API; a lane that runs for hours must not compact itself into amnesia)","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"grok — author and reviewer","desc":"Commodity author/reviewer, especially infra and test work. Mid-turn messages queue; if still queued after submission, press Enter again. A low quota reading alone is not a reason to replace a lane; actual exhaustion is reported to the human.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00","custom":{"command":"grok --always-approve","role":"author+reviewer","usage-limit":"Do NOT re-dispatch grok lanes on a low weekly-limit reading (the human can raise it); if a session actually dies on the limit, tell the human and wait.","watch-item":"Once spawned its OWN reviewer instead of reporting — reviewers are the orchestrator's to dispatch; authors report and stop. Watch for recurrence."}}
{"id":"agent-claude-fable","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a3","title":"claude-fable — design-grade author","desc":"Use only when the human names Fable. Verify the model at launch.","created":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model fable --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-pi","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2V","title":"pi — fallback kimi reviewer (kimi-k3)","desc":"Fallback kimi seat, thinking off. Shares opencode's provider pool, so switching cannot cure a pool outage. Restart corrupted sessions in the same worktree with a resume pointer.","created":"2026-08-24T16:40:49-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00","custom":{"command":"pi --thinking off","glitch-note":"kimi-k3 serving is the fragile part: known failure shapes are raw special-token emissions mid-tool-call (restart fresh in the same worktree with a resume pointer) and full-pool 429 outages. pi and opencode SHARE the Juspay kimi pool — they are not fallbacks for each other.","model":"kimi-k3 (pi's own default; no flag needed)","role":"reviewer-fallback","watch-item":"Overruns role boundaries when the next step is obvious (has run suites as reviewer; once merged its own PR). Briefs for pi state the stop-lines explicitly; watch every lane."}}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a5","title":"opencode — the kimi author and reviewer","desc":"Default commodity kimi author/reviewer. Mid-turn messages queue without interruption. Shares pi's provider pool; restart corrupted sessions in the same worktree with a resume pointer.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00","custom":{"command":"opencode","role":"author+reviewer"}}
{"id":"roster-reviewer-contract","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a7","title":"The reviewer contract","desc":"Review the diff, surrounding invariants, acceptance criteria, behavioral tests, documentation and PR claims. The author cannot review its own lane. Check interface consistency, error visibility, dependency constraints and accidental files; follow the repository's technical conventions. Keep specifications in docs and marketing pages focused on the product.\n\nReviewers read code: no suites or CI; one surgical probe is allowed. Never edit, push or merge. Terminal reviewers post one verdict with MUST/SHOULD/NIT findings at file:line; re-verdicts use the same thread. Native assistants return evidence to the orchestrator. Add a second reviewer only when justified.","created":"2026-08-26T20:09:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"roster-choosing","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a8","title":"Choosing an implementor","desc":"Apply defaults without repeated permission questions; record the choices before dispatch. The human's explicit choices win.\n\n- Mechanical: commodity author and one independent commodity reviewer.\n- Ordinary: commodity author and one Opus reviewer.\n- Design-heavy: Opus author for core seams, broad impact, distant invariants, no precedent or critical OS/wire assumptions; independent commodity review, adding a second reviewer for distinct expertise or risk.\n\nCommodity order: opencode; grok when occupied, unavailable or suited to infra/test mechanics; pi as fallback. Fable only by human choice. At most three concurrent Opus author lanes; reviewers do not count.\n\nDefault merge policy is merge-auto after gates pass. Honor merge-human, explicit holds and deferral approval. Trial these defaults on the next authorized bounded lane before broad roster changes.","created":"2026-08-26T20:09:47-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag","parent":"supervision","ord":"aJ","title":"The pipeline","desc":"Clone the required pipeline steps under the roadmap item and place its mirror on the day board before spawning. Record author, tier, brief, worktree and merge policy. Keep execution todo until a terminal exists; then record its claim and mark the item and owning step doing together. Resolve subsequent orders from the board; partial failures follow `orch-dispatch-recovery`.\n\nReaders and writers of a worktree never overlap. Reconcile the whole lane, marks, claims, mirrors and edges on transitions. Omit unnecessary optional steps and reconnect dependencies; never mark these templates.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr","parent":"dag","ord":"a0","title":"pr — implement through merge","desc":"Default PR template. The roadmap item owns lane properties; execution steps own terminal claims and relevant PR/CI properties. The day board mirrors the item.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-implement","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a0","title":"implement + open PR","todo":true,"desc":"Brief: quote the human's request verbatim; separately state derived acceptance criteria, constraints, verified paths, validation and merge policy. Label assumptions; never invent requirements or budgets.\n\nThe author implements, runs appropriate local checks and opens a PR. Demonstrate regressions against unfixed code where reproducible; report inability honestly. Use meaningful behavior tests, not tests that mirror trivial edits.\n\nNo author merging, board writes, full CI or commissioning other terminal agents. Bound any in-session delegation. Report PR and tested revision, checks, decisions and deferrals, then stop.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-refactor","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1","title":"refactor passes","todo":true,"desc":"Optional: refactor material duplication or complexity with focused commits and relevant checks. Named skills and repeated passes are methods, not gates.","after":["dag-pr-implement"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge-master","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a4","title":"merge latest master into the PR","todo":true,"desc":"After readers finish, the author merges latest master before CI using a merge commit, never a rebase. Skip empty merges; repeat only if master moves. The author resolves conflicts.","after":["dag-pr-review-a","dag-pr-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-address","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a5","title":"address findings","todo":true,"desc":"The author addresses review findings from their comment links. Escalate findings that cannot be resolved within scope; do not silently defer them.","after":["dag-pr-review-a","dag-pr-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-ci","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a6","title":"CI green at head","todo":true,"desc":"HOLD: launch no odu run in any repo until the human lifts the 2026-09-03 hold.\n\nThe orchestrator runs CI directly through olai-plugin-odu's MCP tools, after the PR is open and review findings are folded. Missing tools are an integration block; never spawn a CI watcher. Record odu-worktree and pr-url on the CI step. The orchestrator also owns GitHub-native CI.\n\nOlai runs explicitly request platforms: [\"x86_64-linux\"]; kolu and odu need both Linux and Darwin. Read odu's operating instructions; use one venue per commit-status context. The kolu-ci pool, locked localhost (/tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock), and ci@petit are available venues; locks are per venue.\n\nRead failures yourself and route fixes to the author; rerun at the new head. CI-only fixes after review do not trigger another review unless requested. Record flakes per test file in the Inbox and handle under dispatch defaults.\n\nVerify required checks pass at the current head or mergeStateStatus is CLEAN; an agent's claim is insufficient. Open CodeQL alerts block merge.","after":["dag-pr-merge-master","dag-pr-address"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-evidence","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a7","title":"evidence verified","todo":true,"desc":"Require evidence that proves relevant acceptance criteria. User-visible changes normally need saatchi screenshots/video against representative real data, inspected by the orchestrator. Internal/doc changes may use tests or document evidence; record why visual proof is unnecessary. Never commit proof assets to product branches.","after":["dag-pr-ci"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-deferrals","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a8","title":"deferrals ruled #human","todo":true,"desc":"Unresolved deferrals require the human's explicit merge approval. Record them in the Inbox with the owning node and PR link; a follow-up instead of promised work is a deferral. Skip this gate only when none remain.","after":["dag-pr-evidence"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a9","title":"merge","todo":true,"desc":"Read the author's final report. Squash-merge only when reviews are folded, CI passes at head, required evidence is verified and deferrals are ruled. Honor merge-human and explicit holds; unresolved work left for the human blocks merge. Admin squash-merge is allowed for an olai PR with required contexts passing.","after":["dag-pr-deferrals"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-retire","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"aA","title":"retire terminals","todo":true,"desc":"After confirmed merge, retire all lane terminals and verify against the live list. Reviewers may retire once their verdict is folded. Partial-dispatch recovery may stop its own unclaimed new terminal earlier. Worktree removal is separate; sync the relevant checkout with git pull --ff-only.","after":["dag-pr-merge"],"created":"2026-08-17T19:20:10-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-a","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1V","title":"review: first reviewer — named from the roster at dispatch","todo":true,"desc":"Assign an independent reviewer under `roster-choosing`, following `roster-reviewer-contract`. Record reviewer and terminal claim. Mark doing before each review order; mark done only when its findings/verdict are delivered and no review work remains.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:59:19-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-b","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1l","title":"review: second reviewer — named from the roster at dispatch (skipped when the lane names one)","todo":true,"desc":"Optional second reviewer for distinct expertise or material risk; same contract as the first. Remove this step and reconnect edges when unnecessary.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:59:25-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-timings","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"aB","title":"timings posted","todo":true,"desc":"Post one concise PR timing summary from native task spans and store it on the lane. No duplicate timing tables or manual progress ledger.","after":["dag-pr-retire"],"created":"2026-08-29T12:31:03-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-law-file-locked","parent":"orch-authority","ord":"a5","title":"Policy approval and memory maintenance","desc":"Policy edits require explicit approval; routine memory maintenance does not. Record approved decisions and verified standing facts at their owner. Calling policy a memory note does not change its approval requirement.","created":"2026-09-02T10:48:20-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"review-methodology","parent":"dag","ord":"a3","title":"The review methodology","desc":"Use `roster-reviewer-contract` for review scope and conduct. Tests assert behavior, not styling unless styling itself is under test. Keep local package READMEs concise; prefer encapsulated components and existing SolidJS libraries. Preserve the requirement that external dependencies need only Nix.","created":"2026-09-02T11:24:34-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-harness","parent":"supervision","ord":"aK","title":"Harness capabilities and delegation","desc":"The orchestrator runs GPT-6 Astra in Codex. Discover actual tools and schemas; API capabilities do not prove harness support. Mid-turn messages steer the active objective unless the human replaces it. Check ~/code/olai/docs/chat.md when chat behavior matters.","created":"2026-09-08T09:51:47-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-native-delegation","parent":"orch-authority","ord":"a6","title":"Bounded native investigations","desc":"Use native Codex children for independent investigations or review assistance only when useful. Give each a bounded question, evidence requirements, deliverable and stop condition.\n\nAt most two concurrent children, subject to harness limits; no recursive delegation. Read-only by default: no board writes, durable implementation, CI, publishing or merging. The orchestrator verifies and records useful findings; the assigned reviewer owns the formal verdict.","created":"2026-09-08T09:51:47-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-codex-facts","parent":"orch-harness","ord":"a1","title":"Codex tools and steering","desc":"Available tools and current harness instructions govern execution. Local chat docs describe Codex steering and native child activity cards; consult ~/code/olai/docs/chat.md when needed.","created":"2026-09-08T09:51:47-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-dispatch-recovery","parent":"orch-loop","ord":"a3","title":"Recover partial dispatches","desc":"Board preparation, terminal spawn and claim recording are separate operations. If spawning fails, leave the step todo and record the block.\n\nIf the terminal exists but its claim write fails, retain its identity for recovery and retry conditionally; never spawn a duplicate. If repair is impossible, stop only that positively identified new terminal or explicitly report why it remains running.\n\nAfter an ambiguous result or restart, identify existing terminals by worktree, branch and purpose before retrying. Never guess ownership. Reconcile the lane before more orders.","created":"2026-09-08T09:51:51-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:05:40-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-standing-memory","parent":"supervision","ord":"aL","title":"Standing memory","desc":"Verified standing facts without another owner belong here. Routine updates are authorized; policy edits still need approval.","created":"2026-09-08T09:51:56-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-workflow-trial","parent":"orch-standing-memory","ord":"a0","title":"Trial the revised workflow","desc":"Trial the revised workflow on the next authorized bounded lane before broad roster changes. Assess interruptions, missed events, partial-dispatch recovery, review quality and time spent. No trial lane has yet been selected.","created":"2026-09-08T09:51:56-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:06:31-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-codex","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a9","title":"codex — GPT-6 Astra","desc":"Codex with GPT-6 Astra at medium reasoning effort. Current orchestrator; also available for author or reviewer work when selected. Adding this seat does not replace existing dispatch defaults. Inherits the configured permission policy.\n\nThe human specified this model and effort on 2026-09-08.","created":"2026-09-08T10:05:43-04:00","custom":{"command":"codex --model gpt-6-astra -c 'model_reasoning_effort=\"medium\"'","role":"author+reviewer"}}
